## THE EIGHT QUESTIONS
1. **Do the two locks hold on both apps in every cell, so that open mode can exist ONLY on UAT with the switch on?** (r2) Switch on/off x marker present/absent (and wrong) x platform name x key x each app, plus the API's extra refusals. Open mode reaching the demo, dev or production is a Blocker.
2. **Is the web-to-API assertion unforgeable and bounded?** (r3) HMAC-SHA256, constant-time compare, the 60-second window, replay, expiry, wrong key, wrong level, tamper; no unsigned variant; the API host is directly on the internet (RELAYED brief:33).
3. **Are exactly five routes refused to everyone in open mode, and no other route newly refused or newly reachable?** (r4)
4. **Is the demo provably inert?** (r5) Switch off: today's behaviour; `/api/auth/uat` 404 on a demo-configured run; `/workspace` still needs sign-in; the demo's compiled template.
5. **Do the start-page words match, word for word, the words the product owner approved?** (r6) Card `hpsmpoc-uat-start-page-words-1021` = a, board time 15:12:13 per ADDENDUM-1 (the card store's own `ruled_ts` reads 15:12:54: say which you read).
6. **What can a hostile visitor do?** (r7) Forge or replay an assertion, reach the API directly, escalate level, open-redirect via `next`, cookie flags, cross-site POST, and the open item FOR TUESDAY 8 (a demo-audience Entra token).
7. **Does it render and work in a real browser, in the project's style?** (r8)
8. **Whole suites vs base, mutants, CI, CodeQL, merge.** (r1, r9, r11, r12)

