## TRAPS
- **T-a (lock table is the gate's own).** Build the matrix from D2's TEXT (B409 brief:68) and the code's refusal list, not from the builder's cells. Web: generate `resolveAuth(env)` cases over switch {unset, empty, `off`, `on`, `ON`, `on `, `yes`, `1`, `true`} x `HPSM_ENVIRONMENT` {unset, `uat`, `UAT`, `uat `, `demo`, `dev`, `production`} x platform {none; `WEBSITE_SITE_NAME` = `app-hpsmpoc-web-uat-x`, `...-demo-x`, `uat` (no dashes), empty; only `WEBSITE_HOSTNAME`; only `IDENTITY_ENDPOINT`} x key {absent, 31 bytes, 32 bytes, 32 chars of 2-byte code points, 31 chars of 2-byte (62 bytes), Key Vault reference} x `AUTH_SECRET` {absent, 31, 32, Key Vault reference} x Development header {unset, set}, with an oracle you write from the rule text; assert `uat` appears in exactly the cells the oracle says and in no other, and that every non-`uat` cell equals what the same env gives at BASE (`-base` worktree: the mode is today's). API: the same matrix through `UatOpenAuthentication.Read` and, for a sample of cells (all hosted ones), through a real host start (`WebApplicationFactory` or `dotnet` start) asserting the start-up exception for every refused cell and a clean start for the open cell. **Controls:** a planted weakener per lock (switch ignored, label ignored, site tie dropped, trim added/removed, byte vs char length) must flag the first affected cell; a wrong oracle must be flagged the other way. Record the web/API trim asymmetry cell and say which direction it fails (web open, API closed = safe; the reverse is not possible here, prove it).
- **T-b (assertion is the gate's own).** Mint with your own HMAC from the shape text (do not import the builder's `mintAssertion` for the negative rows; use it only to prove it matches your independent encoding). Time-boundary rows on the API's clock (a fixed `TimeProvider`): exp at now+0, now-29, now-30, now-31 s; iat at now+29, +30, +31; life 59, 60, 120, 121; exp = iat; exp < iat. Plus: wrong key by one bit; each field tampered with the old signature; `v2`; level `Admin`, `ADMIN`, `partner ` (trailing space), `owner`, `root`, empty, 17 chars; 255/256/257 chars; 10 KB; control chars, NUL, CR/LF; non-ASCII digits (`[0-9]` and `NumberStyles.None`); two header lines; one header with a comma-joined pair; header name case; bare `X-Uat-Assertion: v1.admin`; a valid Entra-shaped bearer PLUS a bad assertion (must be 401, no fall-through) and a valid assertion plus a garbage bearer (record). The oracle for "valid" is yours.
- **T-c (route table is the gate's own).** Enumerate every `RouteEndpoint` of the head host (verb, pattern, name, policy, `DestructiveAction` metadata) and of the BASE host, by a probe in `wt-b415-probe`; diff them: the only differences are the five metadata marks and any routes the diff adds (expected none). Then call EVERY route once as the Admin assertion in open mode against a scratch SQLite host and record status and error code: no route other than the five answers `uat.action-off`. Independently of the builder's walker, list every DELETE and every POST/PUT whose name or path contains reset, erase, delete, purge, wipe, truncate, export, personal-data, and classify each as marked, soft-allowed (clearResponse, removeActionItem, discardActionPlan, revokeFollowUp, endClientSession: RELAYED STATUS:33) or UNCLASSIFIED; an unclassified destructive route is a finding. Control: a planted route is found.
