## SEVERITY FLOOR (binding)
- **Blocker:** open mode reachable in any cell outside (`uat` label + switch on + on a platform a `-uat-` site) on EITHER app, or the demo, dev or any non-UAT shape serving the start page or accepting an assertion; any assertion the API accepts that this key did not sign, or whose level is not one of the four, or that confers more than that level's one role; a bare or unsigned header that authenticates; a destructive route of the five that reaches its handler in open mode; any other destructive route found unclassified and reachable as Admin without being on the PR's list (the builder's list is the floor, not the ceiling: if you find a sixth, it is a Blocker unless the product owner's ruling covers it); a browser value that reaches the API assertion header; an off-site or unvalidated `next` at any sink; the shared key in a response, log, client bundle or evidence; a secret in an added line; an existing test weakened, skipped, edited or deleted beyond the builder's named edits; a path in the diff outside the 23.
- **Major:** a lock cell that is wrong on the closed side for the UAT stand-up in a way that cannot be explained (UAT would not open when it should: report, do not loosen); any other route newly refused; a words diff greater than 0 against the card for the heading, intro, four sentences or the blocked-action sentence; a rendered colour or contrast pair off the style guide; an open CodeQL alert at the head (fix in code); a new test red at the head, a name lost, `typecheck`, `lint` or `build` rc != 0, a failed test in the whole suite; a survivor of your mutants on a lock, the signature, the expiry or a refusal; a demo-shape result different from base (other than the named settings); the builder's "21 of 21" not reproducible by a gate-built set; a demo-audience Entra token accepted by the UAT-configured API that reaches a route or role the start page does not already give every visitor AND can change data (the five refusals stand regardless).
- **Minor:** a surviving own mutant of covered behaviour with no equivalence argument; replay inside the window accepted (stateless design: no nonce store) when the window is as stated and the assertion never leaves the server-to-server hop; no server-side revocation after sign-out (an Admin level is free to every visitor anyway; the finding is that the Entra path's F-1 property is not carried); the API accepting a longer life (120 s + 30 s skew) than the web mints (60 s); the web trimming `HPSM_ENVIRONMENT` where the API does not; a Key Vault reference to `uat-open-key` on the demo app; the display names not on the card; a demo-audience Entra token accepted by the UAT API where it adds no reach (the measurement is the finding; the decision is the product owner's); CodeQL pending (conditional verdict, never a bare GO); the `5 KB` `fitsSession` style limits on a new cookie not tested.
- **Note:** the Admin sentence naming "reset and erase" while export, resetShowcase and deleteCustomer are also refused; an unauthenticated caller gets 403, not 401, on the five routes; a POST with neither Fetch-Metadata nor Origin allowed on the choose route (login CSRF on a no-credential site); the shared per-level rate limits; reviewers' own entries visible to the next visitor of that level; STATUS:44 "25 rows" against 23; `SHA2-256` spelling; the red `web build` audit step when new-advisory and not touched; the known timing flake; hosted behaviour UNMEASURED.

## VERDICT
